-- title:
--   Stalks of X×_ℤSpec O have dimension at most two
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and write $\mathfrak{X} =$ `DRModel p` for the two-chart integral model over $\mathbb{Z}$ attached to the modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull p` and its element `IgusaScheme.jFull p`, that is, the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebras of that field generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$; `DRModel.toBase p` is the induced morphism $\mathfrak{X}\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ obtained by descent from the two structure maps. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be equipped with a term of `DRModelPackage p`, a structure bundling: properness and flatness of `DRModel.toBase p`, integrality of `DRModel p`, integral closedness of the sections over every affine open, curve models over $\mathbb{Q}$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with isomorphisms onto the corresponding base changes of $\mathfrak{X}$ and compatibilities of places with the Galois action, two sections of `DRModel.toBase p` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, and a distinguished open smooth locus of relative dimension one containing every open on which the projection is smooth (these data are summarised here). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring, i.e. a commutative ring that is a domain and a discrete valuation ring. Then for every point $z$ of the scheme-theoretic pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z}\to O$, the Krull dimension of the stalk of the structure sheaf of that pullback at $z$ is at most $2$. No condition is imposed on $z$: the bound holds at generic, special and crossing points alike.
--
--   This is the basic dimension bound for the arithmetic surface $\mathfrak{X}_O = \mathfrak{X}\times_{\mathbb{Z}}\operatorname{Spec} O$ obtained from the Deligne–Rapoport model by base change to a discrete valuation ring: each chart becomes integral over a polynomial ring in one variable over $O$, whence dimension at most two. It is used in the analysis of points of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$ and in the construction of the resolved model package and its charts.
